							"Crepuscularity Lite: a GPUI + V8 desktop shell for hosting crepus templates as native apps."
						a href="./docs/lite.html" no-underline text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text hover:opacity-85 border-b crepus-t-border transition-colors inline-block self-center sm:self-start
							"Crepuscularity Lite guide →"
				div w-full min-w-0 mx-auto lg:mx-0 lg:place-self-center order-last lg:order-none min-h-[400px]
					div rounded-xl border overflow-hidden shadow-xl crepus-t-border crepus-t-card
						div flex items-center gap-2 px-3 sm:px-4 py-2.5 sm:py-3 border-b crepus-t-border bg-[var(--cp-code)]
							span flex gap-1.5 shrink-0
								span w-2.5 h-2.5 sm:w-3 sm:h-3 rounded-full opacity-50 bg-[var(--cp-muted)]
								span w-2.5 h-2.5 sm:w-3 sm:h-3 rounded-full opacity-40 bg-[var(--cp-muted)]
								span w-2.5 h-2.5 sm:w-3 sm:h-3 rounded-full opacity-30 bg-[var(--cp-muted)]
							span text-xs font-mono crepus-t-muted ml-1 truncate
								"terminal"
						pre font-mono text-[11px] sm:text-[13px] leading-relaxed p-3 sm:p-4 m-0 crepus-t-pre whitespace-pre overflow-x-visible
							"# New desktop app
$ crepus new my-app && cargo run

# WASM site (this page)
$ crepus web build --manifest docs-site/crepus.toml

# Browser extension
$ crepus webext new ext

# LVGL panel XML
$ crepus build lvgl"

		section py-10 sm:py-14 border-t crepus-t-border crepus-entrance crepus-e3
			div flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:items-stretch gap-5 sm:gap-6 lg:gap-8
				div flex-1 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-8 crepus-t-card
					p text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest crepus-t-muted mb-3 sm:mb-4
						"Native UI from one source"
					p text-lg sm:text-xl font-medium crepus-t-text leading-relaxed mb-4 sm:mb-5
						"Aurorality transforms .crepus templates into native SwiftUI views for macOS and iOS — no WebView, no JavaScript bridge."
					p text-sm crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
						"Semantic tags like navigationstack, sidebar, list, and menu compile to their SwiftUI equivalents. Add eventSink callbacks for app-state integration, wire Rust backends through UniFFI, and hot-reload through the same crepus dev pipeline that serves GPUI and WASM targets."
				div flex-1 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-8 crepus-t-card
					p text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest crepus-t-muted mb-3 sm:mb-4
						"SwiftUI Engine"
					pre font-mono text-sm m-0 leading-relaxed crepus-t-pre p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-lg whitespace-pre-wrap overflow-x-auto
						"navigationsplitview\n  sidebar\n    section header=\"Conversations\"\n      for conv in {conversations}\n        item @click=\"select:{conv.id}\"\n          span \"{conv.title}\"\n  detail\n    vstack gap-3 p-4\n      textfield bind=draft placeholder=\"Message\"\n      button button-prominent @click=\"send\"\n        \"Send\""
				div flex-1 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-8 crepus-t-card
					p text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest crepus-t-muted mb-3 sm:mb-4
						"Capabilities"
					div flex flex-col gap-3
						div flex items-start gap-3
							span text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-snug mt-0.5
								"•"
							div
								p text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text m-0
									"Semantic native tags"
								p text-xs crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
									"navigationstack, sidebar, form, picker, sf-*, and more — all compile to direct SwiftUI views."
						div flex items-start gap-3
							span text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-snug mt-0.5
								"•"
							div
								p text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text m-0
									"macOS chrome"
								p text-xs crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
									"Root-level menubar and dockbadge for native menu commands and dock badges."
						div flex items-start gap-3
							span text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-snug mt-0.5
								"•"
							div
								p text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text m-0
									"Hot-reload IR & swiftgen"
								p text-xs crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
									"crepus dev pushes JSON IR updates or re-runs swiftgen on save — same dev loop as every other target."
						div flex items-start gap-3
							span text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-snug mt-0.5
								"•"
							div
								p text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text m-0
									"Rust ↔ Swift bridge"
								p text-xs crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
									"Plug Rust backends through UniFFI with eventSink wiring for shared state models."
					div mt-4 sm:mt-5
						a href="./docs/aurorality.html" no-underline text-sm font-medium crepus-t-text hover:opacity-85 transition-colors border-b border-transparent hover:border-[var(--cp-accent)]
							"Aurorality guide →"

		section py-10 sm:py-14 border-t crepus-t-border crepus-entrance crepus-e4
			div flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:items-stretch gap-5 sm:gap-6 lg:gap-8
				div flex-1 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-8 crepus-t-card
					p text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest crepus-t-muted mb-3 sm:mb-4
						"Why it's different"
					p text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold crepus-t-text leading-snug mb-4 sm:mb-5
						slot-rotate interval={3000} slot-lede
							"Hot-reloadable templates on GPUI."
							"No JS bundler for extensions."
							"Compile-time view! or full runtime parse."
							"Ship static dist/ to any CDN."
					p text-sm crepus-t-muted m-0 leading-relaxed
						"The same parser and evaluator back the macro, the WASM renderer, and the dev server — so what you author is what ships."
					div mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border px-3 py-1.5 crepus-t-card crepus-t-text text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em]
						span w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[var(--cp-accent)] shrink-0
						"One workspace"
					p text-sm crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed mt-4 mb-0
						"Crepuscularity is a compiler surface, runtime surface, and target manifest in one workspace. Templates stay declarative, target-specific renderers stay explicit, and the CLI keeps build outputs reproducible across app shells, websites, extensions, terminals, panels, and generated UI artifacts."
				div flex-1 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Shared AST"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"Indent and JSX-style input parse into the same node tree, so components, control flow, includes, slots, and defaults travel together."
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Target manifests"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"`crepus.toml` describes build outputs for web, webext, native IR, LVGL, and embedded snapshots without splitting the project model."
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Runtime or compile time"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"Use `view!` when the UI is static, or parse templates at runtime when includes, hot reload, or external files matter."
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Renderer contracts"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"Each backend maps the same template semantics into its native output: GPUI styles, HTML, Ratatui widgets, JSON IR, RGB565, or XML."
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Framework-owned docs"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"Markdown guides and this landing page are built by the same docs-site pipeline, so the public site exercises the framework it documents."
					div rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-5 crepus-t-card
						h3 text-sm font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
							"Small host boundary"
						p text-xs crepus-t-muted leading-relaxed m-0
							"Apps keep ownership of state, event loops, firmware drivers, and platform APIs while Crepuscularity owns template parsing and rendering."

		section py-10 sm:py-14 border-t crepus-t-border crepus-entrance crepus-e5
			h2 text-lg font-semibold crepus-t-text mb-2
				"Three ways to write the same tree"
			p text-sm crepus-t-muted mb-2 max-w-2xl m-0
